LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Margin"
English margin appeared in Book 1 as a percentage of sales. Here it appears as an amount per unit, and the two senses sit a paragraph apart: a contribution margin of $4.80 is money, a contribution margin ratio of 40 per cent is a rate. The exam uses both and distinguishes them only by the word ratio. Arabic هامش المساهمة carries the same ambiguity and relies on نسبة for the rate. French is the clearest of the three: marge sur coûts variables for the amount, taux de marge for the rate, and the word taux makes the distinction impossible to miss. The practical rule for an answer is to write the unit and let no figure stand without one.
